Subject: [PATCH] Make the implementation constructors constexpr

An implementation's constructor only stores its name, description and
required instruction sets, all constants, so it can be `constexpr`. With
it, a program built for one implementation can hold that implementation
as a constant object of its own `final` class and call its methods
directly: the object is initialized when the program is built, no
dynamic initializer runs at startup, and no call goes through the
virtual table or `get_active_implementation()`. The base constructor and
every architecture's are `constexpr`, except rvv's, which asks the
processor whether it has Zvbb.
---
diff --git a/include/simdutf/implementation.h b/include/simdutf/implementation.h
index e936665..6cddb32 100644
--- a/include/simdutf/implementation.h
+++ b/include/simdutf/implementation.h
@@ -7508,9 +7508,9 @@ protected:
    * @param required_instruction_sets the instruction sets this implementation
    * requires
    */
-  simdutf_really_inline implementation(const char *name,
-                                       const char *description,
-                                       uint32_t required_instruction_sets)
+  simdutf_really_inline constexpr implementation(
+      const char *name, const char *description,
+      uint32_t required_instruction_sets)
       : _name(name), _description(description),
         _required_instruction_sets(required_instruction_sets) {}
 
diff --git a/src/simdutf/arm64/implementation.h b/src/simdutf/arm64/implementation.h
index a189e94..0afacd7 100644
--- a/src/simdutf/arm64/implementation.h
+++ b/src/simdutf/arm64/implementation.h
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@ using namespace simdutf;
 
 class implementation final : public simdutf::implementation {
 public:
-  simdutf_really_inline implementation()
+  simdutf_really_inline constexpr implementation()
       : simdutf::implementation("arm64", "ARM NEON",
                                 internal::instruction_set::NEON) {}
 #if SIMDUTF_FEATURE_DETECT_ENCODING
